{"slug":"steven-horsford","qid":"Q3514907","name":"Steven Horsford","desc":"American politician","article":"Steven Horsford","born":"1973-04-29","died":null,"birthplace":"Las Vegas","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NV-04","f":2019,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NV-04","f":2013,"u":2015},{"t":"Nevada Assembly","w":"","f":2004,"u":2012}],"summary":"Steven Alexzander Horsford (born April 29, 1973) is an American politician and businessman serving as the U.S. representative for Nevada's 4th congressional district since 2019, previously holding the position from 2013 to 2015. He also served as chair of the Congressional Black Caucus from 2023 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he served in the Nevada State Senate, representing the 4th district, in Clark County, from 2005 to 2013.","photo":{"f":"steven-horsford.jpg","by":"House Creative Services","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steven_Horsford_118th.jpeg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","n":"Steven Horsford","race":"NV-04"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":174926,"s":52.66,"w":true,"n":"Steven Horsford"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":116617,"s":52.42,"w":true,"n":"Steven Horsford"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":168457,"s":50.67,"w":true,"n":"Steven Horsford"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":121962,"s":51.93,"w":true,"n":"Steven A Horsford"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":59844,"s":45.76,"w":false,"n":"Steven A Horsford"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"NV-04","p":"D","v":120501,"s":50.11,"w":true,"n":"Steven A Horsford"}]}